[[File:Portrait-mode-issue.gif|thumb|Rear cam portrait mode not working due to replacement with different non-programmed sensor.]]
Note: This process applies to iPhone 12 Pro  through iPhone 14 Pro Max (All the Pro Models).

== Problem description ==
On iPhone 12 Pro  through iPhone 14 Pro Max (Pro / Pro Max Series), the LiDAR sensor can stop working due to:

* Drop or physical damage.
* Water/moisture damage affecting the sensor or flex.
* Technician error - failing to transfer the original paired LiDAR sensor when replacing the rear housing. 

== Symptoms ==

* Measure app not working
* Cannot use AR features relying on LiDAR
* In camera app → Portrait mode fails (see fig. 1)
* Sensor missing from diagnostics

== Diagnostic Steps ==

# Open the Measure app → confirm LiDAR cannot detect objects.
# Open portrait mode on rear camera → Confirm it doesn't work.
# Check if rear housing was replaced previously → ask customer .
# If still non-functional → proceed to replacement + reprogramming.

== Repair Steps ==

# Disassembly:  Remove display, disconnect battery. Remove rear camera module. Remove shield covering the LiDAR sensor → take out faulty sensor.
# Brushing unbind & Backing up data: Reconnect display & battery. Connect iPhone to PC. Launch JC Repair Assistant → Read phone. Select Brushing.[[File:Jcid brushing option.png|thumb|Brushing unbind in JCID Repair Assistant software.]]Import firmware → Flash device. If stuck in recovery mode → repeat flash in 3uTools. After brushing unbind and flash is complete, LiDAR sensor data is backed up to the cloud automatically.
# Programming JCID LiDAR sensor: Connect JCID Programmable LiDAR sensor to programmer and write the correct data matching the phone.
# Reassembly:  Install the programmed LiDAR into the iPhone. Reinstall rear camera + shields. Reconnect all flexes and battery.
# Verification: Boot iPhone. Test Portrait mode functions in camera. Open Measure app → confirm proper distance detection.